# Appended at the END of /etc/ufw/after.rules AND of /etc/ufw/after6.rules (root:root, 0640, as
# ufw ships them), then `ufw reload`. ADR-27 (staging rule: no mail leaves the server); SEC-M4I-01.
#
# Docker's published ports and its containers' outgoing traffic pass the FORWARD chain, not ufw's
# INPUT and OUTPUT rules, so `ufw deny out 25/tcp` does not stop a container. Docker sends every
# forwarded packet through DOCKER-USER first: this block rejects a container's connection to the
# mail ports of any other host (SMTP 25, submission 465 and 587, and 2525). Mail inside the
# topology (API and worker to Mailpit on 1025) never leaves the bridge and is not touched.
# `sudo iptables -S DOCKER-USER` and `sudo ip6tables -S DOCKER-USER` show the two rules after
# every reboot (Docker keeps the chain, ufw fills it again on start).
*filter
:DOCKER-USER - [0:0]
-A DOCKER-USER -p tcp -m multiport --dports 25,465,587,2525 -j REJECT --reject-with tcp-reset
-A DOCKER-USER -j RETURN
COMMIT
